        <mxCell id="lIsNepdnBAUAu_AT9RLy-1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;gradientColor=#97d077;strokeColor=#82b366;" value="&lt;b&gt;Tenant Context&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Resolve + inject tenantId&lt;/i&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="150" x="219" y="355" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jNFN7KJj7yrHW0cX2_W_-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Steps&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;This was my process when approaching this design:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Recall the meeting (&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;I was unable to obtain the meeting transcript)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, the flow and the needs discussed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;and write it down.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. Define essential vs optional Azure services based on&lt;br&gt;   the required flows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Choose architecture style based on flow complexity, technologies, SLA, and other factors.&lt;br&gt;   Decision: modular monolith + Azure Functions for async ops.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. Define which strategy to use for a multi-tenant&lt;br&gt;  application.&amp;nbsp;(see Multi-Tenancy diagram)&lt;br&gt;   Decision: shared app tier, isolated database per tenant.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. Choose the database engine based on isolation model,&lt;br&gt;   access patterns and schema flexibility needs.&lt;br&gt;   Decision: pending — see DB* note inside diagram.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6. First architectural diagram&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;and document&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;  the assumptions being made.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="370" width="390" x="1380" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jNFN7KJj7yrHW0cX2_W_-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Flow&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remembered flow (interview notes)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Client → uploads documentation&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;→ sent to external data center&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;→ response received from data center&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;→ generate a package of files&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;→ format and present output to the user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Implemented as:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. Client&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. APIM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. Entra ID (auth + tenant resolution)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;4. Tenant Context (inject tenantId)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;5. Document Ingestion (validate, store to Blob,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;publish message)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6. Service Bus (sessionID = tenantId)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;7. External DC Caller (submit, receive jobId)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;8. External Data Center process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9. DB* (write JobId + status &quot;Pending&quot;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;10. Status Checker (timer trigger, poll DC)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;11. DB* (update jobId + Status)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;12. External Data center check status&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;13. Service Bus (trigger package builder)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;14. Package Builder (assemble output)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;15. DB* / Blob (write Processed Output)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;16. Notification Dispatcher (write New Notification)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;17. DB* (notification record)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;18. Notification Module reads on user request&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;19. Output Renderer reads on user request&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="820" width="470" x="1380" y="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jNFN7KJj7yrHW0cX2_W_-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Assumptions&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;I took the liberty of making these assumptions with the sole purpose of showing a complete flow and demonstrating my way of working:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Flow and scope&lt;br&gt;   Document processing and tenant onboarding are the two flows in scope.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Async processing / SLA&lt;br&gt;   The external data center has unknown and potentially long response times.&lt;br&gt;The flow is async by design.&lt;br&gt;   The client submits documents and receives a notification (email or in-app) when processing completes.&lt;br&gt;   No processing time SLA is defined.&lt;br&gt;   A polling pattern is used. the Status Checker runs on a timer trigger and asks the DC if the job is done.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. External data center&lt;br&gt;   Assumed to be a single shared REST API endpoint for all tenants. Each job returns a jobId on submission and exposes a status endpoint to check completion.&lt;br&gt;   If tenants have individual endpoints or credentials, per-tenant secrets in Key Vault accommodate this without architectural changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. Output package&lt;br&gt;   It is unknown whether the external DC response produces a file package (stored in Blob) or structured data (persisted to DB*). The diagram models the boundary only.&lt;br&gt;   Final model depends on the external DC response format.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. Formatting and views&lt;br&gt;   Output presentation is tenant-configurable with a default view. Users may override the tenant default. View templates are stored per-tenant in DB*.&lt;br&gt;   Output is rendered inside the application on demand, no push to external systems assumed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6. Notification delivery&lt;br&gt;   The Notification Dispatcher (async pipeline) writes the notification record to DB*.&lt;br&gt;   The Notification Module (monolith) reads and serves it when the user requests it.&lt;br&gt;   No real-time push (SignalR) is required at this stage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;7. Document volume&lt;br&gt;   Volume per tenant is assumed moderate. No chunked upload, streaming processing or parallel worker scaling is required at this stage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;8. Availability&lt;br&gt;   Single geographic region. Availability target applies to business hours in that region. No 24/7 or&lt;br&gt;   multi-region requirement is assumed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;9. Compliance&lt;br&gt;   Data residency, GDPR and industry-specific compliance are not addressed in this version. The architecture does not preclude adding them, isolated databases and Key Vault are compatible with most compliance frameworks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="750" width="520" x="1890" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jNFN7KJj7yrHW0cX2_W_-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DB*&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;The database engine has not been defined yet.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;This decision depends on information not available&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;at this stage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two candidates:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Azure Cosmos DB&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Flexible schema — each tenant can have different&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;document structures without migrations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Native per-tenant database isolation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Document-oriented model fits the output&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;package well&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; - Higher cost at low volume&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; - Eventual consistency requires careful design&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; - Different query model from SQL -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;team learning curve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Azure SQL&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Familiar to most .NET teams&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Strong consistency and mature tooling&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; + Lower cost at moderate volume&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; - Schema changes across tenant databases require&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;coordinated migrations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; - Less flexible if tenant document structures&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;diverge significantly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Decision drivers&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; → How structurally different are tenant schemas?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; → What are the query patterns on processed output?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; → What is the team&#39;s existing experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;with SQL vs NoSQL?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note: both options are compatible with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;isolated data tier model. This decision does not&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;affect the overall architecture, only the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;implementation of the data layer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="720" width="510" x="1890" y="800" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="clMeWjgdrVV1SJ5eQIS_-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#b0e3e6;strokeColor=#0e8088;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="50" x="990" y="30" as="geometry" />
